      {
        "id": 90521,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-10T20:19:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Envisioner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Envisioner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I contend that it is impossible for any but the simplest effects (and questionably even those) to be \"simultaneous\".&nbsp; Certainly not a card play, nor even damage type changing.&nbsp; And there can be issues even with damage adjustment, as with my recent question on Twist the Ether vs. Cramped Quarters Combat.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>\"Simple\" has <strong><em>nothing</em></strong> to due with being \"simultaneous\"</p>\n<p>Multiple effects that change damage type (lets say the +1 vats from Pike Industrial that turn damage Toxic and Ra's Imbued Fire) are absolutely considered simultaneous, so you are very wrong on that count.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Playing a one shot triggers the effects on the card. There are other effects in the game that trigger upon playing a card. Because they have common triggers, the effects nessesarily are simultaneous.</p>\n<p>Does that make sense?</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:15:53.305Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
