      {
        "id": 90522,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-10T20:21:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>If they were \"simultaneous\", then each one would constantly overwrite the other and the game would freeze.&nbsp; They <em>must</em> be consecutive, so that one can trump the other.&nbsp; If you roll them into the OoO ruling, it makes it possible to declare either one as \"high trump\", which does reduce the bookkeeping of which one was in play first, and that's what the OoO ruling was about).&nbsp; But they cannot possibly be \"simultaneous\", any more than two different answers to \"Which day of the week is it\" can both be correct (given that the answer is the name of a day, and not something cutesy like \"Tomorrow\" or \"hump day\").</p>",
