      {
        "id": 90523,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-10T20:23:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Envisioner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Envisioner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If they were \"simultaneous\", then each one would constantly overwrite the other and the game would freeze.&nbsp; They <em>must</em> be consecutive, so that one can trump the other.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>No dude, thats why the Order of Operations rule is in place. Players choose how those effects resolve.</p>\n<p>Edit:Everything else you wrote is nonsensical so I wont address it.</p>",
